WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.044
To break the data bottleneck, the authors built USIS10K,

00:00:04.124 --> 00:00:09.273
the first large-scale underwater salient instance
segmentation dataset.

00:00:09.353 --> 00:00:14.575
It contains 10,632 underwater images, each with
pixel-level annotations,

00:00:14.655 --> 00:00:17.962
spanning seven categories from diverse scenes.

00:00:18.042 --> 00:00:22.160
The authors analyze it carefully: instances per category,

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:24.517
instance distribution per image,

00:00:24.597 --> 00:00:29.966
and global versus local color contrast against the
prior SIS10K benchmark,

00:00:30.046 --> 00:00:34.827
showing underwater imagery poses distinct
low-contrast challenges.

00:00:34.907 --> 00:00:36.668
Beyond training USIS-SAM,

00:00:36.748 --> 00:00:42.780
USIS10K gives the whole community a foundation for
underwater salient segmentation.
